  "id": "one-tailed-test",
  "term": "one-tailed test",
  "definition": "A one-tailed test is a significance test that looks at the probability of a result as extreme as the observed one in only one specified direction, such as values greater than a hypothesized value. It is used when the question concerns change or difference in a single direction rather than either direction.",
